WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:09.160
Hi everyone, I'm Rachel.

00:09.160 --> 00:11.160
Kimi Work is our local agent.

00:11.160 --> 00:13.560
It's like an AI teammate on your computer.

00:13.560 --> 00:19.200
It can work directly with your files, browser, and everyday tools to help you get things done.

00:19.200 --> 00:22.760
If you use Kimi on the web, you probably know the usual flow.

00:22.760 --> 00:27.040
Upload a file, wait for Kimi to finish, and then download the result.

00:27.040 --> 00:29.440
With Kimi Work, it's much simpler.

00:29.440 --> 00:33.680
Just tell Kimi where the file is, and it can read and edit it directly.

00:33.680 --> 00:37.200
When it's done, the results stay right on your computer.

00:37.200 --> 00:39.960
In this video, we'll start by installing Kimi Work.

00:39.960 --> 00:47.240
Then I'll show you around, walk you through the basics, and introduce a few advanced features for more complex tasks.

00:47.240 --> 00:55.560
The video is divided into chapters, so feel free to jump to the part you need, or stay with me, and we'll go through it together, step by step.

00:55.560 --> 00:57.960
First, let's get Kimi Work set up.

00:57.960 --> 01:03.960
Go to Kimi.ai, click Kimi Work on the sidebar, and follow the instructions to install it.

01:03.960 --> 01:11.200
Once it's installed, sign in with your Kimi account, and you're ready to get started.

01:11.200 --> 01:15.920
Once you open Kimi Work app, you'll see two tabs, chat and work.

01:15.920 --> 01:20.160
Chat works just like Kimi on the web, and your history stays in sync.

01:20.160 --> 01:23.920
Today, we're focusing on the work, so go ahead and select it.

01:23.920 --> 01:27.920
Let's take a quick look at the interface.

01:27.920 --> 01:32.920
On the far left, you'll find features including dashboards, plugins, and schedule tasks.

01:32.920 --> 01:37.160
Below is your history, where your projects and conversations are saved.

01:37.160 --> 01:41.920
Before we move on, let's look at a few settings worth knowing about.

01:41.920 --> 01:42.920
One is permissions.

01:42.920 --> 01:47.920
This determines whether Kimi Work needs your approval before it takes action.

01:47.920 --> 01:49.920
Another is model and thinking level.

01:49.920 --> 01:55.920
For more complex tasks, you can choose a higher thinking level, but it will take longer.

01:55.920 --> 01:59.920
Here, we can start by selecting K3 High.

01:59.920 --> 02:04.920
To start a new task, click the Create button beside Project and choose a folder.

02:04.920 --> 02:08.920
You can use an existing folder or create a new one.

02:08.920 --> 02:11.920
The folders become KimiWorks workspace.

02:11.920 --> 02:16.920
It can read the files inside, edit existing files, and create new content.

02:16.920 --> 02:19.920
Now, let's try a simple task together.

02:19.920 --> 02:21.920
Organizing a project folder.

02:21.920 --> 02:25.920
We can ask Kimi to read every file and sort them by content.

02:25.920 --> 02:30.920
Put duplicate or outdated files into a review folder and give us a summary when it's done.

02:30.920 --> 02:40.920
We can see Kimi opens each file, work out what it's for, organize the folder as requested, and send us the result.

02:40.920 --> 02:43.920
But what if the information you need isn't stored locally?

02:43.920 --> 02:48.920
Sometime, you need to look it up in a browser or sign into an account before you can access it.

02:48.920 --> 02:51.920
That's when you can use Kimi browser extension.

02:51.920 --> 02:54.920
Once you've installed it by following the instructions,

02:54.920 --> 02:58.920
KimiWorks can work directly within the page in your browser.

02:58.920 --> 03:03.920
For example, it can browse feeds, find social media trends and insights,

03:03.920 --> 03:05.920
or help you fill out online forms.

03:05.920 --> 03:08.920
Now, let's go beyond the browser.

03:08.920 --> 03:11.920
KimiWorks can also use other apps on your computer.

03:11.920 --> 03:13.920
Once computer use is installed and enabled,

03:13.920 --> 03:19.920
Kimi can understand what's on your screen and handle actions that will normally require a mouse and a keyboard,

03:19.920 --> 03:23.920
including clicking, scrolling, and typing.

03:23.920 --> 03:28.920
From sending a message or printing a file to working on complex software,

03:28.920 --> 03:31.920
you can hand all kinds of tasks over to KimiWork.

03:31.920 --> 03:40.920
For example, before a product launch, you can ask Kimi to follow a checklist, test each feature, and record any issues it finds.

03:40.920 --> 03:43.920
Kimi follows the same step as a real user would.

03:43.920 --> 03:47.920
It opens a feature and works through the entire flow.

03:47.920 --> 03:50.920
From files to browser to the rest of your computer,

03:50.920 --> 03:54.920
KimiWork can take action across more and more of your workspace.

03:54.920 --> 03:59.920
That means more of the work you use to handle yourself can now be handed over to Kimi.

03:59.920 --> 04:05.920
Now we've covered the basic, let's look at a few advanced features for more complex tasks.

04:05.920 --> 04:10.920
So far, we've been working with one agent at a time.

04:10.920 --> 04:14.920
But some tasks are simply too big for one agent to handle alone.

04:14.920 --> 04:17.920
Like converting hundreds of files into the same format,

04:17.920 --> 04:19.920
or putting together a business review,

04:19.920 --> 04:24.920
where sales data, user feedback, and support issues need to be analyzed separately.

04:24.920 --> 04:26.920
That's when you can use agents form.

04:26.920 --> 04:29.920
It's like a team of agents built for your task.

04:29.920 --> 04:31.920
Each agent has its own strength,

04:31.920 --> 04:35.920
and they work together in parallel to complete the projects.

04:35.920 --> 04:37.920
Let's look at an example.

04:37.920 --> 04:40.920
Say I want to research the global semiconductor market.

04:40.920 --> 04:45.920
Finding the data and doing the analysis used to take several days, or even a week.

04:45.920 --> 04:50.920
Now, I can click here and hand the full task over to the agent's form.

04:50.920 --> 04:54.920
Once Kimi received the task, this form divides the work on its own.

04:54.920 --> 05:03.920
Some agents collect and organize data, some test strategies, other analyze risk, combine the findings, and write the report.

05:03.920 --> 05:15.920
An hour later, I have an analysis of 100 semiconductor stocks based on 10 years of data, 5 strategies to consider, and a complete research report, and with public presentation.

05:15.920 --> 05:21.920
Instead of relying on one agent to do everything, you now have a whole team working together.

05:21.920 --> 05:26.920
That makes even larger, complex tasks much more manageable.

05:26.920 --> 05:32.920
Agents form helps with large tasks by splitting the work across a team of agents.

05:32.920 --> 05:34.920
Goal works differently.

05:34.920 --> 05:39.920
You can give Kimi a clear result to work towards, along with the standards you need to meet.

05:39.920 --> 05:43.920
Kimi then keeps working, tracking, and improving the result until it's done.

05:43.920 --> 05:46.920
Let's say you want to make a small game.

05:46.920 --> 05:49.920
Writing the first version of code is only the beginning.

05:49.920 --> 05:54.920
Before the game is truly finished, it needs to be tested and improved again and again.

05:54.920 --> 05:58.920
This is exactly the kind of task Goal is designed for.

05:58.920 --> 06:04.920
Kimi can build, check its work, and make changes until the results meet your requirements.

06:04.920 --> 06:07.920
To use it, type a slash and select Goal.

06:07.920 --> 06:10.920
A good Goal should clearly cover three things.

06:10.920 --> 06:17.920
What you want Kimi to make, what it should check before finishing, and any rules you need to follow.

06:17.920 --> 06:25.920
Here, I'm asking Kimi to build a 3D retro arcade that runs on the browser and includes four classic games.

06:25.920 --> 06:31.920
Before it finishes, Kimi needs to play each game and make sure everything runs smoothly with no errors.

06:31.920 --> 06:36.920
I've also added one design rule. No neon or cyberpunk elements.

06:36.920 --> 06:41.920
Once the Goal is set, you don't need to look at the test window or review every version.

06:41.920 --> 06:44.920
Kimi will build, test, and fix the result on its own.

06:44.920 --> 06:48.920
As long as it hasn't met the requirements, it will keep going.

06:48.920 --> 06:52.920
A regular task may finish in 10 or 20 minutes.

06:52.920 --> 06:55.920
With Goal, Kimi can keep working for hours.

06:55.920 --> 06:57.920
Here's the final result.

06:57.920 --> 07:05.920
If we compare it with earlier version, we can see the visuals becoming more polished and the games becoming more playable with each round.

07:05.920 --> 07:11.920
Good tools help people work more efficiently, and the same is true for agents.

07:11.920 --> 07:14.920
Now, let's give Kimi the right tools.

07:14.920 --> 07:16.920
Plugins are like tool kit for Kimi work.

07:16.920 --> 07:20.920
Click Plugins on the left to open the plugin marketplace.

07:20.920 --> 07:23.920
There are two types of plugins in Kimi work.

07:23.920 --> 07:25.920
The first is connectors.

07:25.920 --> 07:35.920
They let Kimi connect to and use the apps you already work with, including Google Workspace, Notion, Obsidian, Blender, Trepo, etc.

07:35.920 --> 07:37.920
The second is expert skills.

07:37.920 --> 07:42.920
They cover areas like financial analysis, software development, and design,

07:42.920 --> 07:46.920
and show Kimi how to handle those specialized tasks.

07:46.920 --> 07:48.920
Many tasks also need reliable data.

07:48.920 --> 07:55.920
Kimi connects to professional data sources, including WINT, scientific databases, and academic research databases.

07:55.920 --> 08:07.920
On the skills page, you will also find more ready-made workflows for specific tasks, such as organizing meeting notes, polishing presentation, and converting citation formats.

08:07.920 --> 08:08.920
Let's install them.

08:08.920 --> 08:12.920
Just find the plugin you need in the marketplace and click install.

08:12.920 --> 08:17.920
Then click use or type a slash in the chat box to quickly open any plugin you've installed.

08:17.920 --> 08:21.920
If you can't find the right plugin, you can build your own.

08:21.920 --> 08:25.920
Type a slash, choose plugin builder, and describe what you need.

08:25.920 --> 08:34.920
You can build one from an open source project, connect it to a third-party app, or turn a workflow you use often into a reusable plugin.

08:34.920 --> 08:38.920
With plugins, Kimi can take a bigger role in your day-to-day work.

08:38.920 --> 08:47.920
It can read documents from the tool you already use, pull in data from professional databases, organize the final material, and email them to a client.

08:47.920 --> 08:52.920
We'll keep adding to the plugin library, so you can come back and see what's new.

08:52.920 --> 08:55.920
A good coworker does more than getting the job done.

08:55.920 --> 08:57.920
They also learn how you like to work.

08:57.920 --> 09:00.920
Agents.md helps Kimi do the same.

09:00.920 --> 09:05.920
Think of Agents.md as a set of standing instructions for Kimi work.

09:05.920 --> 09:11.920
Each project folder or conversation can have its own file, so Kimi knows how to handle that type of work.

09:11.920 --> 09:14.920
And you don't need to write it from scratch.

09:14.920 --> 09:21.920
Just tell Kimi about the work, the rules they should follow, the plugins they should use, and the final output you want.

09:21.920 --> 09:25.920
Kimi can turn those requirements into an Agents.md for you.

09:25.920 --> 09:31.920
As you can see, Kimi creates an Agents.md for you and saves it to the right project folder.

09:31.920 --> 09:36.920
If anything changes later, you can edit it yourself or ask Kimi to update it.

09:36.920 --> 09:41.920
With Agents.md, future tasks become much easier.

09:41.920 --> 09:46.920
Just tell Kimi what you want to do, and it will automatically follow the same instructions.

09:46.920 --> 09:50.920
Dashboard can help you keep up with the things that matter in your everyday work.

09:50.920 --> 09:52.920
It brings everything into one place.

09:52.920 --> 09:55.920
Click Dashboard on the left, and you'll see two examples.

09:55.920 --> 09:57.920
One is Daily Finance Dashboard.

09:57.920 --> 10:02.920
It brings market news, stock prices, and industry heat map onto one page.

10:02.920 --> 10:04.920
Each part is a widget.

10:04.920 --> 10:10.920
You can move and combine them, delete the ones you don't need, or ping them to your desktop for easier access.

10:10.920 --> 10:14.920
Simply put, anything you want to follow can become a widget.

10:14.920 --> 10:16.920
It doesn't have to be work data.

10:16.920 --> 10:22.920
Your calendar, habit tracking, daily news, or even a playlist can all become widgets.

10:22.920 --> 10:25.920
Put them together, and you have a dashboard of your own.

10:25.920 --> 10:31.920
To make a dashboard of your own, click the plus button on the top and tell Kimi work what you want to follow.

10:31.920 --> 10:35.920
It will help you build the dashboard step by step, through conversations.

10:35.920 --> 10:37.920
And that's your tour of Kimi work.

10:37.920 --> 10:40.920
I put everything we've covered into a mind map.

10:40.920 --> 10:43.920
Feel free to take a screenshot and save it for later.

10:43.920 --> 10:47.920
There's a lot here, so don't worry about remembering everything at once.

10:47.920 --> 10:53.920
And if anything is so unclear, you can also download Kimi work and ask it directly.

